      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #84): 0⋆B checked only b.real() == 0.0 to
      ⍝ decide "B is 0" and return 1, so any purely-imaginary B (0⋆0J1,
      ⍝ 0⋆0J¯1) or a B with real part 0 but a nonzero imaginary part
      ⍝ (0J0⋆0J1) wrongly gave 1 too. 0⋆B is 1 only for B exactly 0J0;
      ⍝ for any other B with a non-positive real part it is undefined
      ⍝ (0⋆¯1J1 already correctly gave DOMAIN ERROR, for comparison).
