      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(o)): bif_power_ci()'s exact-repeated-
      ⍝ multiplication path (used for |exponent| ≤ 1024) squared first
      ⍝ and inverted afterwards for a negative exponent, so the
      ⍝ intermediate squaring could already overflow to infinity (here
      ⍝ (1E200)² = 1E400) even though the true, inverted result is
      ⍝ finite -- unlike the real (non-complex) path, which already
      ⍝ handles this correctly (Bugs27 #23).
      ⍝
      1E200J0*¯2
0

      1E200*¯2
0

      ⍝ control: an ordinary, non-overflowing case is unaffected
