¯0.0112J¯0.0384

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #10): 0J1⋆N (or 0J¯1⋆N) for an
      ⍝ integer N above the exact-repeated-squaring cutoff (1024) fell
      ⍝ through to complex_power()=exp(N×ln a), whose N×π/2 intermediate
      ⍝ loses precision as N grows, corrupting even an exactly
      ⍝ representable unit-circle result. 0J1/0J¯1 are now recognized as
      ⍝ exact fourth roots of unity and computed from N mod 4 directly,
      ⍝ for any magnitude of N.
      ⍝
      ⎕PP←17

